; `parallel` binds each name ONCE, at its join, so `mut` on a binding
; has nothing to mean and is a PARSE error at the word rather than a
; silent acceptance the checker then has to refuse. `.axbad` because a
; parse error stops the file, so this case carries exactly one
; malformed form.
(import IO)

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main) (parallel p ((mut a 1)) a))
